# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in. Never commit the real file.
#
# Foundry connection settings are NOT here: fill in ../fvtt-mcp-dnd5e/.env first. The scribe
# reads that file through fvtt-mcp-dnd5e's client library (loadEnv), for the host FOUNDRY_HOST
# selects (molten | local):
#   FOUNDRY_URL          the Foundry server's URL
#   FOUNDRY_WORLD_ID     the world to expect
#   FOUNDRY_WAKE_URL     molten only: the link that wakes a sleeping hosted box
# (and the older MOLTEN_* / LOCAL_* aliases of those). FOUNDRY_USER / FOUNDRY_PASSWORD there are
# the bridge's login and are NOT used: the scribe joins as FOUNDRY_SCRIBE_USER below. The admin
# key there is stripped: the scribe can wake a host, never launch a world. To read a different
# file than ../fvtt-mcp-dnd5e/.env, set FVTT_MCP_ENV (an absolute path) here or in the
# registration's env.

# The scribe's own Foundry login. Create this Assistant GM user in the world first, or name an
# existing one (never the bridge's user: two clients on one user double Battle Flow's
# automation). The sandbox mirrors prod's users.
FOUNDRY_SCRIBE_USER=Scribe Assistant
FOUNDRY_SCRIBE_PASSWORD=

# The campaign repo the session record is written to (campaign.json at its root), an absolute
# path. Machine-local, so it lives only in .env.
SCRIBE_CAMPAIGN_REPO=

# Python with faster-whisper (built by scripts/setup.ps1). Default shown.
# SCRIBE_PYTHON=%USERPROFILE%\.session-scribe\venv\Scripts\python.exe

# Headless browser for PDFs. Default: Microsoft Edge's standard install path.
# SCRIBE_EDGE=C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft\Edge\Application\msedge.exe
